// The enforcement half of the decorated-declaration fix: a `private` on an
// @extern declaration must actually restrict it, not merely parse.
//
// This is the test that would have caught the shape the fix replaced. The
// decorator branch of parse_stmt passed a hardcoded "public" to
// parse_fun_decl_with_doc, so a modifier written before the decorator was
// dropped on the floor — the file compiled clean and exported the name anyway.
// A parse test alone would have been satisfied by that.
//
// `_abs_after` uses the annotation-then-modifier order; test/pass/
// visibility_decorated.sf covers the other order working legally.
import "../support/visibility_decorated.sf" as Decorated

IO.println(Decorated._abs_after(-1))
